---
slug: mcp-admin/reject-principal
method: post
---
{%- comment -%}
  Operator bulk-rejects EVERY pending approval for one principal (spec §9.6, §12.4).
  Complements the per-principal approval-queue cap: the cap bounds inflow, this
  drains a flooder's queue in one action instead of N reject clicks. Each rejected
  action never runs; the decision is recorded per row. Operator-gated. Bounded to the
  newest 50 pending rows for the principal (the cap keeps a single principal far below
  that; a larger backlog drains over repeated clicks rather than in an unbounded loop).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  function current_profile = 'modules/user/helpers/current_profile'
  # platformos-check-disable UnreachableCode
  # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag
  include 'modules/user/helpers/can_do_or_unauthorized', requester: current_profile, do: 'mcp.admin', redirect_anonymous_to_login: true, forbidden_partial: null, access_callback: null, anonymous_return_to: '/mcp-admin', entity: null
  # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag
  # platformos-check-enable UnreachableCode

  assign pid = context.params.principal_id
  if pid != blank
    graphql f = 'modules/mcp/approvals/pending_by_principal', principal_id: pid, per_page: 50
    for a in f.records.results
      # Bulk drain: one claim per pending row is inherent — mutations can't be
      # batched into a single query here. Bounded to the first 50 rows. Each goes
      # through approval/claim so a row an operator is approving concurrently is
      # never flipped to rejected mid-execution.
      function _c = 'modules/mcp/commands/approval/claim', id: a.id, handle: a.handle, status: 'rejected', decided_by: current_profile.user.id, result_summary: 'Bulk-rejected by operator (queue drain).'
    endfor
  endif

  redirect_to '/mcp-admin?tab=approvals'
-%}
